I have a fantastic decision to tell you about
that was made by a panel of judges in North

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:08.180
Carolina.

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:14.179
Now it's just one decision and it is a much
broader problem gerrymandering than one decision

00:00:14.179 --> 00:00:19.460
can fix, but this is the right decision that
was made and that's what matters in this particular

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:20.460
case.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:27.210
The way that Republicans drew the district
lines in North Carolina does not quote permit

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:33.100
voters to freely choose their representative
according to Superior Court decisions that

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:38.650
have been, uh, filed and the districts cannot
remain drawn this way.

00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:44.530
The maps according to this ruling in North
Carolina were specifically drawn, no surprise.

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:51.370
We've known this for years to maintain a republican
super majority in the state legislature.

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:53.760
This is what North Carolina Republicans are
known for.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:58.830
This is what North Carolina Republicans have
been doing and succeeding with for a very

00:00:58.830 --> 00:00:59.830
long time.

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:04.519
Now, there's an interesting sort of legal
circumstance here that's important to understand.

00:01:04.519 --> 00:01:08.280
You might remember that just a few months
ago, the Supreme Court ruled that you cannot

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:15.170
challenge partisan gerrymandering in federal
court and yet here we have a superior court

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:16.520
making this decision.

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:21.850
But there is a rule in the North Carolina
constitution called the free elections clause,

00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:26.009
which specifically says you cannot do partisan
gerrymandering.

00:01:26.009 --> 00:01:32.070
Partisan gerrymandering according to the North
Carolina Constitution is um, uh, unconstitutional.

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:36.409
And that is what led to this decision being
made in North Carolina.

00:01:36.409 --> 00:01:40.049
Even though conceivably if it had been appealed
or attempted to be appealed up to the Supreme

00:01:40.049 --> 00:01:44.170
Court, the Supreme Court would not have taken
up a given their prior decision in June.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:48.179
So the right decision in North Carolina, we
know that this has been going on.

00:01:48.179 --> 00:01:51.420
What happens now with the districts in North
Carolina.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:02:00.959
Um, there is a deadline until September 18
lawmakers will have to redraw new maps, which

00:02:00.959 --> 00:02:06.859
if they are fairly redrawn, they could give
Democrats a chance to actually do some damage

00:02:06.859 --> 00:02:11.910
in the North Carolina state legislature in
2020 and hopefully pick up some seats.

00:02:11.910 --> 00:02:16.310
If Democrats can pick up the majority in the
North Carolina state legislature in November

00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:23.000
of 2020 then they will be in charge of drawing
the maps after the 2020 census in 2021 which

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:24.030
would be great.

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:28.860
But again, this is where Democrats and Republicans
where left and right are not the same.

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:34.280
I have no interest in Democrats taking over
the majority in the North Carolina state legislature

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:41.330
in November of 2020 and then redrawing districts
in a completely unfair away that benefits

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:42.330
Democrats.

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:46.640
Now you could say it would be a just outcome
because Republicans have done it for nearly

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:51.030
the entire period between the 2010 and the
2020 census.

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:56.140
Republicans in North Carolina deserve to have
the lines redrawn in a way that favors Democrats

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:57.620
instead of Republicans.

00:02:57.620 --> 00:02:59.190
We don't need to cheat to win.

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:01.060
I just want fair maps.

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:07.060
Fair maps are what I want, not diferently
unfair maps that now benefit Democrats.

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:13.940
Uh, when it comes to a lot of these issues,
I am not looking to reverse the structural

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:18.970
advantage that Republicans have unfairly created
for themselves and create it for the left.

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:23.530
I just want fair maps because I know that
with fair maps and voter turnout, meaning

00:03:23.530 --> 00:03:26.780
everybody is allowed to vote, who wants to
vote and their votes are counted.

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:29.490
I know that that's enough for us to win.

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:35.250
Uh, however, it's completely plausible that
the maps that are redrawn in North Carolina

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:42.110
between now and September 18th, 18th, will
simply be slightly less, obviously unfair

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:45.760
to Democrats, but still heavily slanted towards
Republicans.

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:47.510
That's a realistic possibility.

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:52.480
One of the things about gerrymandering is
that there's a huge incentive to do it even

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:58.420
if it later is going to be tossed out because
people who were elected under gerrymandered

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:00.870
districts don't lose their seats.

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:06.020
If the districts are found to have been gerrymandered
and the map has to be changed, your election

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:09.230
under a gerrymandered map doesn't become null
and void.

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:12.990
If the district maps are later determined
to be unconstitutional, which is why they

00:04:12.990 --> 00:04:13.990
keep doing it.

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:20.400
You have a census in 2010 the next year they
draw bonkers crazy districts.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:23.889
They win seats, they maintain a super majority.

00:04:23.889 --> 00:04:30.310
Then they can actually push what they want
in terms of bills becoming law for one election

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:32.169
for two elections, whatever.

00:04:32.169 --> 00:04:36.430
Meanwhile, Democrats have to fight them in
court on the way the districts were drawn

00:04:36.430 --> 00:04:41.150
and then if a few years later the districts
end up being tossed out.

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:43.830
You picked up the seats, the winters were
there.

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:48.180
They got to pass bills, they got to make laws
and then you get the keep those seats.

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:52.300
Even if the judge says that the districts
ultimately have to be redrawn, this is the

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:55.539
evil genius of partisan gerrymandering.

00:04:55.539 --> 00:05:01.050
Even if you later lose the other side has
to spend a ton of time and money fighting

00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:05.979
the drawing of the districts and you get to
keep all of those seats that the gerrymandering

00:05:05.979 --> 00:05:07.360
helped you win in the first place.

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:08.610
That's why it's so pernicious.

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:13.999
This is why the census matters so much and
this is why we need a, there are models.

00:05:13.999 --> 00:05:21.800
There are endless academicians who have put
together models for how you should draw districts.

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:22.800
Computers can do it.

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:28.030
You don't need people saying, let's shift
